```javascript
function isPrime(n) {
  if (n < 2) return false;
  if (n === 2) return true;
  if (n % 2 === 0) return false;
  for (let i = 3; i * i <= n; i += 2) {
    if (n % i === 0) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

Returns `true` if `n` is prime, `false` otherwise.

The function checks divisibility only up to the square root of `n` (since any factor larger than √n has a corresponding factor smaller than √n). It skips even numbers after checking for 2. For `n = 1000000`, this runs in milliseconds instead of looping to the full number.
